
=== versions
npm 10.9.7 on node v22.22.2
npm 11.21.3 on node v22.22.2
npm 12.2.3 on node v22.22.2

=== 1. What npm says about a global prefix with a UUID in its path (<scratch>/p-0b7e5a2c-3f1d-4c6e-9a8b-1234567890ab, from the user's .npmrc)
--- npm 10.9.7
npm prefix -g        → <scratch>/p-0b7e5a2c-3f1d-4c6e-9a8b-1234567890ab
npm root -g          → <scratch>/p-0b7e5a2c-3f1d-4c6e-9a8b-1234567890ab/lib/node_modules
npm config get prefix → (exit 1) npm error The prefix option is protected, and can not be retrieved in this way
npm exec -c (child)  → <scratch>/p-0b7e5a2c-3f1d-4c6e-9a8b-1234567890ab
--- npm 11.21.3
npm prefix -g        → <scratch>/p-***
npm root -g          → <scratch>/p-***/lib/node_modules
npm config get prefix → (exit 1) npm error The prefix option is protected, and cannot be retrieved in this way
npm exec -c (child)  → <scratch>/p-0b7e5a2c-3f1d-4c6e-9a8b-1234567890ab
--- npm 12.2.3
npm prefix -g        → <scratch>/p-***
npm root -g          → <scratch>/p-***/lib/node_modules
npm config get prefix → (exit 1) npm error The prefix option is protected, and cannot be retrieved in this way
npm exec -c (child)  → <scratch>/p-0b7e5a2c-3f1d-4c6e-9a8b-1234567890ab

